// Ch10 B03 "The dead channel" (C, 1 min). F03: a still pool under a great dead mangrove: bare bleached
// crown, black wet roots, nothing green. The egrets leave on the cut (sound only). O05: a dozen small pale
// lights caught in the roots, HELD: cyan, perfectly still, neither sinking nor rising. Pell softly hums
// the storm's note (his tell: overwhelmed). Then the roots move: the flow starts the Drowner's battle.
title: ch10_dead_channel
location: ch10/ossa_fen
---
@letterbox on
@sfx egret_lift
@camera F03
@music silence fade=2.0
@wait 2.5
@camera O05
@vfx glimmer_held at=drowner_roots count=12 rate=slow
@wait 2.0
@sfx pell_storm_note at=pell vol=0.4
Pell [sad]: Three of the clutch. Drowned here. At the full moon before last. #line:ch10_channel_001
Asha [worried]: They're still here. #line:ch10_channel_002
Pell [neutral]: Held. #line:ch10_channel_003 #tn:"Kirru word for the dead who cannot lift: kept down, not resting."
@wait 1.0
@anim mangrove_drowner stir
@wait 1.0
@letterbox off
===
